The runtime image and the module archives that are built from this repository contain the
following third-party software as separate jar files or Java modules. Each keeps its own license.

In the runtime image (lib/, the daemon and the command line):
- Jackson (annotations, core, databind, dataformat-toml) 2.22 - Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson
- picocli 4.7.7 - Apache License 2.0 - https://picocli.info
- sqlite-jdbc 3.53 (Xerial) - Apache License 2.0; it contains SQLite, which is in the public domain
  https://github.com/xerial/sqlite-jdbc
- The Java runtime that jlink put together (OpenJDK) - GNU General Public License 2 with the
  Classpath Exception; its legal notices are in the directory legal/ of the image
  https://openjdk.org

In lib/praksis/expression (the expression layer, one jar with its dependencies inside):
- CEL-Java 0.15.0 (Google) - Apache License 2.0 - https://github.com/google/cel-java
- Protocol Buffers for Java - BSD 3-Clause License - https://protobuf.dev
- Guava, Guava failureaccess and listenablefuture (Google) - Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/google/guava
- Error Prone annotations, J2ObjC annotations, AutoValue annotations (Google) - Apache License 2.0
- RE2/J (Google) - BSD 3-Clause License - https://github.com/google/re2j
- ANTLR 4 runtime - BSD 3-Clause License - https://www.antlr.org
- ThreeTen-Extra - BSD 3-Clause License - https://www.threeten.org/threeten-extra
- SnakeYAML - Apache License 2.0 - https://bitbucket.org/snakeyaml/snakeyaml

In lib/praksis/modules/maildir (the module, and the HTML library of every mail module):
- jsoup 1.22.1 - MIT License - https://jsoup.org

What is used only to build and test (JUnit, AssertJ, GreenMail, TestFX) is not part of what is
shipped. The mail modules that need Eclipse Angus Mail are in Praksis-Modules-Mail, which lists them.
